  "articleBody": "Applying drywall compound looks straightforward until light hits a finished wall at an angle, exposing lumps, dips, and seam lines. Knowing when to bring in an experienced finisher saves time and material.\n\nSigns It Is Time to Call a Professional:\n- Long runs of flat seams and butt joints: Butt joints lack tapered edges, requiring wide feathering to keep seams unnoticeable.\n- Visible tape bubbling or edge peeling: When tape separates from base compound, joints must be opened and bedded again correctly.\n- Outside and inside corner bead alignment: Crooked corner beads make baseboards and door casings sit out of square.\n- High-visibility walls under direct sunlight: Critical lighting across long walls highlights minor ridge lines that require skilled hand tooling.\n- Post-settlement drywall joint cracking: Repeated cracks along structural framing require evaluation to secure backing before re-mudding.\n\nWhat to Prepare Before You Start\nNote room temperature, identify areas where seams feel uneven, and clear floor spaces along baseboards. For dependable drywall taping, mudding, and full-scope residential remodeling throughout the Denver area, contact owner Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC. Call 303-505-0866 or reach out via coloradoremodeling.company to schedule your project estimate.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
